diff --git a/crates/rightkit-oauth/CHANGELOG.md b/crates/rightkit-oauth/CHANGELOG.md
index 72188cc..eebaa62 100644
--- a/crates/rightkit-oauth/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/crates/rightkit-oauth/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,5 +1,15 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## 0.8.1 (unreleased)
+
+Orthic-Labs/rightkit#194 (CodeRight follow-ups), #697, #700. Additive: nothing existing changed in signature or behaviour, except that `exchange_code` now also checks the PKCE verifier shape and a non-empty `redirect_uri` without whitespace (always true for requests from `begin_loopback`). New opt-in `async` feature (`rightkit-http/async`); `rightkit-http` is not enabled for async by default. Not built or run locally.
+
+- #194: `OAuthClient::exchange_code_with_verifier(code, &Secret, redirect_uri)` exchanges a pasted code with a caller-held PKCE verifier, so the manual-paste fallback needs no `AuthorizationRequest`; `OAuthClient::refresh_token(&Secret)` refreshes from a bare refresh token (rotated token returned, else the one passed in); `refresh` delegates to it. Mastodon/X presets, the keychain store and durable pending store were already in 0.7.0.
+- #194/#697: with the `async` feature, `OAuthClient::{exchange_code_async, exchange_code_with_verifier_async, refresh_async, refresh_token_async}` and `GatewayExchange::{exchange_async, exchange_tokens_async, exchange_raw_async, refresh_async}` take a `rightkit_http::AsyncClient` (its address policy and proxy apply). They share request building and answer parsing with the blocking calls.
+- #697: `GatewayExchange::new_allowing_insecure_host(endpoint, host)` and `GatewayExchange::allow_insecure_host(host)`: explicit, exact-host opt-in to plain `http://` for an operator-configured non-loopback gateway (default off, `https://` unaffected, no wildcard, scheme, port or path in the host).
+- #700: `CallbackListener::wait_post_json_with(timeout, cancel, allowed_origin, validate)`; `wait_post_json` is `wait_post_json_with(.., |_| Ok(()))`. `validate` runs after the origin, path and `state` checks; `Err(text)` is answered `400` with `text` and the wait continues.
+- Tests: `tests/verifier_exchange.rs`, `tests/async_calls.rs` (feature `async`), `post_json_with_rejects_a_body_before_acknowledging_it`, `plain_http_needs_an_explicit_exact_host`.
+
 ## 0.8.0 (2026-10-17)
 
 Orthic-Labs/rightkit#586, #587, #588, #589, #600 (CodeRight and MailRight ports). Additive: every existing call behaves as before; `OAuthConfig`, `CallbackOptions` and `LoopbackHost` keep their shapes, and the new settings sit behind builder methods on private fields. Endpoint URLs are now parsed, not prefix-checked: userinfo, backslashes and whitespace are refused, and plain `http` is accepted only for the exact hosts `127.0.0.1`, `[::1]`, `localhost`. Not built or run locally.
